  It's no wonder you're confused.  Section 16's equivalences (which you
quote) are directly contradicted by section 23's equivalances (X .i
TENSE bo Y = TENSE gi X gi Y = Y TENSE le nu X), which flips the
TENSEgi/gi sense.  There is no errata on this chapter, but I expect the
table in sec. 16 is wrong.
              --gejyspa

